{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Moses.</b> On the pattern of <i>mateh</i> [staff]. In my opinion it is a noun, but according to many it is a participle, like 'owner,' as in 'and wisdom gives life to its owners' [Ecclesiastes 7:12], 'its owner shall take' [Exodus 21:28], and the meaning is: one who has the matter in his possession." "<b>Yasheh [shall remit].</b> A transitive verb, and the lender is called a נושה [creditor] in it." "<b>Yagoash [shall exact].</b> He shall press, like 'and all your bones you shall press' [Deuteronomy 4:9?]. And behold, the nun appears in the future-tense forms of possessors of nun [i.e., verbs whose first root letter is nun]." "<b>A remission for HaShem.</b> For the honor of HaShem, who gave him the wealth. And the reason for the construct state of the mem [in שמטה] before the Name is: 'for it is a sabbath for HaShem.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {2 "The verse cited as וכל עצביכם תנגושו does not correspond to any standard biblical verse; the reference is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:32.609353853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}